  "_comment": "The DENOMINATOR for characterization coverage: the set of Aeneas source sites that reject a legal-Rust construct (the fragment boundary), extracted from craise/save_error messages in /opt/aeneas/src (~40 of 129 total; the other ~89 are internal invariants like 'Unreachable'/'Ill-formed'/'Internal error' and are excluded). Coverage = fraction of these 'msg' substrings a probe run triggers. 'probeable' marks whether the construct is reachable from safe, buildable Rust (false ones are documented in the playbook, not probed). This set is version-locked to the toolchain image; regenerate on a toolchain bump. The separate 'opaque-axiom' failure mode (stdlib without a Lean model) is NOT here — it is governed by the builtin registry (extract/ExtractBuiltin*.ml), enumerated by registry_extract.",
